WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:06.060
&gt;&gt; Okay. So, it is now

00:00:06.061 --> 00:00:09.090
my great pleasure and
an honor to introduce

00:00:09.091 --> 00:00:11.730
our chief guest for
today who will be giving

00:00:11.731 --> 00:00:15.480
a keynote address today,
Mr. Dnyaneshwar Muley.

00:00:15.481 --> 00:00:16.530
I met him at

00:00:16.531 --> 00:00:18.180
the prophecy part of
the adivas that was that was

00:00:18.181 --> 00:00:21.535
organized by India's Ministry
of External Affairs,

00:00:21.536 --> 00:00:26.030
in June this year, focusing
on artificial intelligence.

00:00:26.031 --> 00:00:29.885
Mr. Muley is Secretary to

00:00:29.886 --> 00:00:31.460
the Ministry of External Affairs

00:00:31.461 --> 00:00:33.425
and Indian Overseas Affairs,

00:00:33.426 --> 00:00:36.530
but what I found also very
interesting in addition to

00:00:36.531 --> 00:00:37.760
all his accomplishments in

00:00:37.761 --> 00:00:39.350
the Ministry of
External Affairs is that

00:00:39.351 --> 00:00:41.500
he's a very celebrated author.

00:00:41.501 --> 00:00:43.410
I understand in Marathi,

00:00:43.411 --> 00:00:44.870
but also in Hindi,

00:00:44.871 --> 00:00:46.530
and maybe other languages.

00:00:46.531 --> 00:00:49.190
In addition, he has launched

00:00:49.191 --> 00:00:52.125
educational projects
in his native town,

00:00:52.126 --> 00:00:57.180
and so, it's really a great
honor to have him here today,

00:00:57.181 --> 00:01:00.210
and I look forward to
your remarks, thank you so much.

00:01:00.211 --> 00:01:02.990
&gt;&gt; So, great pleasure
meeting you,

00:01:02.991 --> 00:01:04.520
i have just arrived
from the airport,

00:01:04.521 --> 00:01:07.220
and sorry to be little late.

00:01:07.221 --> 00:01:12.120
Disclaimers first, I'm
not an expert in AI,

00:01:12.121 --> 00:01:14.615
so my position is quit safe.

00:01:14.616 --> 00:01:19.105
I'm also not a representative
today of government,

00:01:19.106 --> 00:01:22.350
any government agency, that's

00:01:22.351 --> 00:01:24.240
why my intelligence today

00:01:24.241 --> 00:01:26.700
is going to be really artificial.

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:30.050
I'm not holding any key,

00:01:30.051 --> 00:01:32.980
some notes yes, but really,

00:01:32.981 --> 00:01:36.005
I don't claim to be
a keynote speaker.

00:01:36.006 --> 00:01:38.860
My interest would be
really I'm a student,

00:01:38.861 --> 00:01:43.745
I'm quite amazed and I'm
no scientific background,

00:01:43.746 --> 00:01:45.940
no IT background, otherwise,

00:01:45.941 --> 00:01:48.685
I would have used
something very high-tech.

00:01:48.686 --> 00:01:51.035
But, I have a deep interest
in this because

00:01:51.036 --> 00:01:54.025
anything that is
game changing interest me,

00:01:54.026 --> 00:01:57.640
anything that can really,
I'm from a village,

00:01:57.641 --> 00:01:58.675
my father was a farmer,

00:01:58.676 --> 00:02:01.395
I joined the foreign service
perhaps by fluke,

00:02:01.396 --> 00:02:04.430
by chance, but my interest
has always been,

00:02:04.431 --> 00:02:07.510
why am I in the foreign service,
type of a question.

00:02:07.511 --> 00:02:10.210
Therefore, I always
try to see whether I

00:02:10.211 --> 00:02:13.430
can connect diplomacy to people,

00:02:13.431 --> 00:02:15.470
that's my focus because diplomacy

00:02:15.471 --> 00:02:17.225
is not Minister of
External Affairs in my view,

00:02:17.226 --> 00:02:19.130
diplomacy is not South block,

00:02:19.131 --> 00:02:22.600
North block, diplomacy is
people, people of a country.

00:02:22.601 --> 00:02:24.580
So, just like that,

00:02:24.581 --> 00:02:27.030
I know AI or no AI,

00:02:27.031 --> 00:02:29.960
it has to be ultimately for
people and for the humanity.

00:02:29.961 --> 00:02:33.890
So, that is the basic concern
and being a student,

00:02:33.891 --> 00:02:37.850
I read a little bit and
there if I feel that this

00:02:37.851 --> 00:02:39.860
is some game changing thing that

00:02:39.861 --> 00:02:42.705
is on the horizon, and therefore,

00:02:42.706 --> 00:02:46.120
we organize this
conference in MEA,

00:02:46.121 --> 00:02:49.855
where we had experts coming
from all over the world,

00:02:49.856 --> 00:02:52.720
and we had some
interesting discussions.

00:02:52.721 --> 00:02:55.330
So, that's where I start,

00:02:55.331 --> 00:02:56.925
I'm not a skeptic,

00:02:56.926 --> 00:03:01.670
I'm not suspicious of what
it will do to humanity.

00:03:01.671 --> 00:03:04.175
Though in the past any measure

00:03:04.176 --> 00:03:06.800
game-changing
technology or effort

00:03:06.801 --> 00:03:10.710
has always been seen
with suspicion.

00:03:11.260 --> 00:03:14.330
Every now and then we

00:03:14.331 --> 00:03:16.700
see a pattern emerge
within technology and

00:03:16.701 --> 00:03:19.535
society at large that there comes

00:03:19.536 --> 00:03:22.580
along a new understanding
that man has of science,

00:03:22.581 --> 00:03:24.350
a new ability to manipulate

00:03:24.351 --> 00:03:26.210
the tools in his environment to

00:03:26.211 --> 00:03:28.390
his benefit to craft

00:03:28.391 --> 00:03:31.285
the world around him
in a new dimension,

00:03:31.286 --> 00:03:34.115
and a new possibility
that didn't exist before,

00:03:34.116 --> 00:03:36.650
and such moments,

00:03:36.651 --> 00:03:39.905
what I called pivot
points change everything,

00:03:39.906 --> 00:03:42.455
they accelerate
the evolution of society,

00:03:42.456 --> 00:03:46.300
accelerate our culture, help
us overcome all problems,

00:03:46.301 --> 00:03:48.170
and create new opportunities,

00:03:48.171 --> 00:03:49.850
there's a paradigm shift that

00:03:49.851 --> 00:03:52.220
these pivot points have

00:03:52.221 --> 00:03:54.300
on society that
becomes undeniable,

00:03:54.301 --> 00:03:57.690
they alter the course
of history forever.

00:03:57.691 --> 00:04:01.395
Some of the pivot points
in history, for example,

00:04:01.396 --> 00:04:06.435
we learned to walk,
man discovers fire,

00:04:06.436 --> 00:04:09.240
innovation of the V,

00:04:09.241 --> 00:04:12.090
we learned to farm,
we learned to build,

00:04:12.091 --> 00:04:13.900
we build the first
pulley systems,

00:04:13.901 --> 00:04:15.120
we build the railroads,

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:16.910
two men realize you can sit in

00:04:16.911 --> 00:04:20.055
a tin can with wings
and it will fly,

00:04:20.056 --> 00:04:22.350
the invention of nuclear power,

00:04:22.351 --> 00:04:25.110
the invention of transistors
and silicon chips,

00:04:25.111 --> 00:04:27.255
the first telephonic
conversation,

00:04:27.256 --> 00:04:30.925
the invention of
the first computer,

00:04:30.926 --> 00:04:33.440
the invention of
the mobile phone,

00:04:33.441 --> 00:04:35.600
the invention of smartphone,

00:04:35.601 --> 00:04:39.620
Facebook, and now man
marveling at its potential to

00:04:39.621 --> 00:04:43.180
be at the cusp of creating
something in its reflection,

00:04:43.181 --> 00:04:45.560
yet, other than itself,

00:04:45.561 --> 00:04:48.980
an intelligence, that is
artificial intelligence.

00:04:48.981 --> 00:04:53.660
Unlike what Hollywood or
fantasy novels would sell you,

00:04:53.661 --> 00:04:57.150
the doomsday scenario of
AI taking over [inaudible]

00:04:57.151 --> 00:05:00.910
to rather paint a much
different grounded view.

00:05:00.911 --> 00:05:03.600
In AI, I see liberation,

00:05:04.130 --> 00:05:07.915
though I'm not quite
100 percent sure.

00:05:07.916 --> 00:05:10.805
While coming here, I
also had this thought of

00:05:10.806 --> 00:05:14.015
this great book by
Francis Fukuyama,

00:05:14.016 --> 00:05:17.615
called the Posthuman Society.

00:05:17.616 --> 00:05:22.130
This I read sometime in 2013,

00:05:22.131 --> 00:05:25.785
and Fukuyama has a very
interesting view of the world,

00:05:25.786 --> 00:05:27.685
some of you might be knowing.

00:05:27.686 --> 00:05:30.875
He says that, we are

00:05:30.876 --> 00:05:35.255
perhaps on the cusp of
being a new species,

00:05:35.256 --> 00:05:37.840
humanity, Posthuman Society is

00:05:37.841 --> 00:05:40.055
the name of this particular book.

00:05:40.056 --> 00:05:44.625
The developments in biotechnology,
genetic engineering,

00:05:44.626 --> 00:05:50.420
robotics, precision
engineering, IT,

00:05:50.421 --> 00:05:54.615
all this is changing humanity
to certain extent that we

00:05:54.616 --> 00:05:56.120
are perhaps likely to become

00:05:56.121 --> 00:05:58.970
a different species all together,

00:05:58.971 --> 00:06:02.545
that's his conclusion,
if I remember correctly.

00:06:02.546 --> 00:06:07.220
Therefore, we need to
have a larger mechanism

00:06:07.221 --> 00:06:08.870
to bring some kind of

00:06:08.871 --> 00:06:13.435
a basic regulatory
framework for this,

00:06:13.436 --> 00:06:17.530
just as we have
a nuclear weapons,

00:06:17.531 --> 00:06:20.000
we have weapons of
mass destruction.

00:06:20.001 --> 00:06:24.020
Some kind of an international
conversation which creates.

00:06:24.021 --> 00:06:26.510
I particularly believe the fact

00:06:26.511 --> 00:06:29.160
that it's good to be a humanity,

00:06:29.161 --> 00:06:31.325
rather than being something else,

00:06:31.326 --> 00:06:33.590
because it's
a great responsibility

00:06:33.591 --> 00:06:36.395
now to remain a human,

00:06:36.396 --> 00:06:39.410
and in that journey,

00:06:39.411 --> 00:06:41.450
I'm actually not sure as to

00:06:41.451 --> 00:06:45.635
how AI will play out its role,

00:06:45.636 --> 00:06:48.980
will it help us in achieving

00:06:48.981 --> 00:06:51.110
a new station in

00:06:51.111 --> 00:06:55.625
the evolutionary process or
will it change us completely?

00:06:55.626 --> 00:06:58.160
I think that AI is

00:06:58.161 --> 00:07:00.760
not specifically mentioned
by Francis Fukuyama,

00:07:00.761 --> 00:07:02.170
if I remember correctly,

00:07:02.171 --> 00:07:03.870
I had not heard this word,

00:07:03.871 --> 00:07:07.140
I know maybe two years back,

00:07:07.141 --> 00:07:08.975
I had not heard this word myself.

00:07:08.976 --> 00:07:10.550
So, that being the case by us

00:07:10.551 --> 00:07:12.435
what he says is now actually,

00:07:12.436 --> 00:07:14.670
we're perhaps facing that moment.

00:07:14.671 --> 00:07:16.305
So, it's very interesting,

00:07:16.306 --> 00:07:17.560
and very fascinating, and

00:07:17.561 --> 00:07:20.570
very challenging moment
for all of us.

00:07:20.680 --> 00:07:24.055
You might wonder why I
bring up this point,

00:07:24.056 --> 00:07:26.960
it is because AI too is
a revolutionary technology,

00:07:26.961 --> 00:07:29.315
one that shine some mirror
right in our face,

00:07:29.316 --> 00:07:32.720
and for it to truly to be
adopted we must ensure it

00:07:32.721 --> 00:07:34.730
permeates our culture in

00:07:34.731 --> 00:07:37.310
a way that touches the
lives of billions.

00:07:37.311 --> 00:07:39.860
Particularly, billions
is a word which very

00:07:39.861 --> 00:07:41.600
suitable for India because

00:07:41.601 --> 00:07:43.800
once I was asked
being a diplomat,

00:07:43.801 --> 00:07:46.415
how would you describe India?

00:07:46.416 --> 00:07:49.190
Actually, everyone has thought

00:07:49.191 --> 00:07:50.960
a lot about one's own country,

00:07:50.961 --> 00:07:52.950
it often becomes
difficult to encapsulate

00:07:52.951 --> 00:07:55.520
it in one sentence
or a few words.

00:07:55.521 --> 00:07:58.815
So, I said India is
1.3 billion stories,

00:07:58.816 --> 00:08:01.840
and when I look back
I always think that's

00:08:01.841 --> 00:08:05.245
a very fairly intelligent answer

00:08:05.246 --> 00:08:09.370
because if you see the
diversity, language, culture,

00:08:09.371 --> 00:08:14.945
folk songs, people,
costumes, heritage.

00:08:14.946 --> 00:08:20.010
It's an absolutely
fascinating playground

00:08:20.011 --> 00:08:22.570
for people in AI because

00:08:22.571 --> 00:08:25.600
AI has to deal with
very complex things,

00:08:25.601 --> 00:08:30.375
including, I think, intuitions
and how do we really come.

00:08:30.376 --> 00:08:32.150
So, India that way is

00:08:32.151 --> 00:08:36.110
a very fertile ground for
this particular purpose.

00:08:36.111 --> 00:08:39.450
Let me clear, I'm not
here to be prophetic or

00:08:39.451 --> 00:08:41.290
simply talk in abstract terms as

00:08:41.291 --> 00:08:43.270
if I'm pitching you a new idea.

00:08:43.271 --> 00:08:47.210
I guess you have already
bought it to the idea,

00:08:47.211 --> 00:08:49.345
which is why we are here.

00:08:49.346 --> 00:08:51.930
I'm here to get
specific about how

00:08:51.931 --> 00:08:54.490
AI can affect daily life and

00:08:54.491 --> 00:08:55.580
what can be done to

00:08:55.581 --> 00:08:59.315
ensure the proliferation
of this great technology,

00:08:59.316 --> 00:09:03.430
so it can truly rise
to its best potential.

00:09:03.431 --> 00:09:05.770
Knowledge is best utilized if

00:09:05.771 --> 00:09:07.755
it becomes a part of daily life.

00:09:07.756 --> 00:09:09.230
That is the true moment of

00:09:09.231 --> 00:09:11.120
pivot point for any technology,

00:09:11.121 --> 00:09:12.350
where it goes from being

00:09:12.351 --> 00:09:14.445
exclusive to becoming
all inclusive.

00:09:14.446 --> 00:09:18.450
Facebook, an extremely
exclusive community.

00:09:18.451 --> 00:09:24.135
At first, meant only for
Harvard grads, truly took off,

00:09:24.136 --> 00:09:25.935
and saw its rise when

00:09:25.936 --> 00:09:27.940
the mithaiwala down
the street could

00:09:27.941 --> 00:09:30.330
also be on the same platform.

00:09:30.331 --> 00:09:33.505
Trust me, he knows
how to use Facebook

00:09:33.506 --> 00:09:37.285
just as well as anybody
else in this room.

00:09:37.286 --> 00:09:41.040
We as humans tend to be

00:09:41.041 --> 00:09:44.600
blind to see well
as anybody else.

00:09:44.601 --> 00:09:48.415
We as humans tend to
be blinded to see,

00:09:48.416 --> 00:09:51.390
there resides in everybody,

00:09:51.391 --> 00:09:53.100
a spark of brilliance,

00:09:53.101 --> 00:09:54.825
whatever you can name it,

00:09:54.826 --> 00:09:59.490
social brilliance or maybe
singing brilliance or talent.

00:09:59.491 --> 00:10:01.530
That brilliance comes
in varied forms.

00:10:01.531 --> 00:10:04.255
For some, it is in
writing a great deal.

00:10:04.256 --> 00:10:07.510
Some, it is creating algorithms.

00:10:07.511 --> 00:10:09.070
For some, it is
building a company.

00:10:09.071 --> 00:10:12.105
For some, it's PhD
from IIT or USC.

00:10:12.106 --> 00:10:14.495
For some, it is
knowing how to run

00:10:14.496 --> 00:10:18.455
the best mithai shop in
the entire Chandni Chowk.

00:10:18.456 --> 00:10:20.360
Yet, all of us are

00:10:20.361 --> 00:10:22.965
brilliant and intelligent
in our own ways.

00:10:22.966 --> 00:10:24.440
If we are supposed to

00:10:24.441 --> 00:10:28.030
truly think of benefit
of AI to the society,

00:10:28.031 --> 00:10:31.725
we have to first internally
accept everyone is brilliant.

00:10:31.726 --> 00:10:35.025
Just because Lalaji
from Chandni Chowk,

00:10:35.026 --> 00:10:37.660
who owns the best
mithai shop in Delhi,

00:10:37.661 --> 00:10:40.295
never learned how to
write his first line of

00:10:40.296 --> 00:10:44.380
code and print
Hello World on C++,

00:10:44.381 --> 00:10:46.815
doesn't mean he lacks
the intelligence to make

00:10:46.816 --> 00:10:49.815
AI a daily part of his life.

00:10:49.816 --> 00:10:52.360
Our friend simply speaks
a different language.

00:10:52.361 --> 00:10:54.715
This transaction
between the scientist

00:10:54.716 --> 00:10:59.350
and Lalaji breaks down if
the scientist puts the onus

00:10:59.351 --> 00:11:04.330
on Lalaji to figure out
how to use AI or to

00:11:04.331 --> 00:11:05.915
know the difference between

00:11:05.916 --> 00:11:09.735
convolutional neural net
and artificial neural net.

00:11:09.736 --> 00:11:16.210
It's like Lalaji asking
a programmer whether to fry

00:11:16.211 --> 00:11:19.640
the badam first or
the kishmish for

00:11:19.641 --> 00:11:23.555
the halwa to retain
the slightly charred,

00:11:23.556 --> 00:11:26.285
but not burnt flavor.

00:11:26.286 --> 00:11:31.765
We just want the halwa and
we want it to taste good.

00:11:31.766 --> 00:11:35.120
When good technology
doesn't get adopted,

00:11:35.121 --> 00:11:36.920
it's a communication
breakdown between

00:11:36.921 --> 00:11:38.870
the scientists and the masses.

00:11:38.871 --> 00:11:43.350
I believe that anything
that we are doing at

00:11:43.351 --> 00:11:44.640
this particular stage in

00:11:44.641 --> 00:11:48.480
our evolution has to be
useful to the masses,

00:11:48.481 --> 00:11:50.470
which really represent nothing,

00:11:50.471 --> 00:11:52.795
but the humanity at its core.

00:11:52.796 --> 00:11:56.410
This happens because many a
times, futuristic technology,

00:11:56.411 --> 00:11:58.050
they tend to become egalitarian,

00:11:58.051 --> 00:11:59.945
reserved only for the elite few.

00:11:59.946 --> 00:12:03.040
So, even if something
may have a great impact,

00:12:03.041 --> 00:12:05.680
the masses learn to shy
away from such tools,

00:12:05.681 --> 00:12:07.790
self subscribing
to the impression

00:12:07.791 --> 00:12:09.750
that a certain tool
or technology may be

00:12:09.751 --> 00:12:12.130
outside their
comprehension or that

00:12:12.131 --> 00:12:15.235
it's something meant to
be in a research lab.

00:12:15.236 --> 00:12:19.760
Often, it is the very creators
who end up isolating

00:12:19.761 --> 00:12:21.520
their own creations
when they become

00:12:21.521 --> 00:12:25.280
subjects of elite praising only.

00:12:25.281 --> 00:12:27.535
With that, technologies,

00:12:27.536 --> 00:12:29.570
which could have had
a wonderful impact,

00:12:29.571 --> 00:12:31.785
end up dying a slow,

00:12:31.786 --> 00:12:34.100
painful death versus
mass adoption.

00:12:34.101 --> 00:12:36.250
I remember that Akio Morita,

00:12:36.251 --> 00:12:37.765
in his Made in Japan,

00:12:37.766 --> 00:12:41.400
also had made some very
interesting points about how

00:12:41.401 --> 00:12:44.140
a video cassette recorder of

00:12:44.141 --> 00:12:47.100
a particular size
survived and how it

00:12:47.101 --> 00:12:50.010
did not because they
thought that they

00:12:50.011 --> 00:12:53.600
wanted to have
an exclusive product

00:12:53.601 --> 00:12:56.860
while everybody else in
the world had adopted

00:12:56.861 --> 00:13:02.045
a particular standard and are
producing mass creations.

00:13:02.046 --> 00:13:04.890
So, I'm here to give you
context of how AI can

00:13:04.891 --> 00:13:07.430
go on to become a
part of daily of

00:13:07.431 --> 00:13:08.700
Indians and hopefully give

00:13:08.701 --> 00:13:11.310
some perspective on why it
is extremely critical for

00:13:11.311 --> 00:13:13.820
AI to proliferate down

00:13:13.821 --> 00:13:15.995
to the very grassroot levels
of the society,

00:13:15.996 --> 00:13:18.760
outside of standard corporate
environment as well.

00:13:18.761 --> 00:13:20.165
It is my hope,

00:13:20.166 --> 00:13:21.600
as we start digging deeper,

00:13:21.601 --> 00:13:23.595
that the ideas and viewpoints,

00:13:23.596 --> 00:13:25.290
I put forth help inspire

00:13:25.291 --> 00:13:28.385
the audience members to
truly think outside the box.

00:13:28.386 --> 00:13:31.530
For AI proliferation to
happen at the highest level,

00:13:31.531 --> 00:13:33.255
we must design AI tools

00:13:33.256 --> 00:13:35.400
such that one is able
to use them without

00:13:35.401 --> 00:13:37.600
requiring any prerequisite tools

00:13:37.601 --> 00:13:40.180
or knowledge or even skills.

00:13:40.181 --> 00:13:41.685
Let me give you an example.

00:13:41.686 --> 00:13:44.780
There was a time
designing a website was

00:13:44.781 --> 00:13:48.540
something you hired a coder for.

00:13:48.541 --> 00:13:50.410
It was a luxury afforded only to

00:13:50.411 --> 00:13:54.370
the few lucky ones who were
either affluent enough to

00:13:54.371 --> 00:13:57.990
have a website or were
literate enough to

00:13:57.991 --> 00:14:01.830
navigate the world of CSS,
HTML, or Dreamweaver.

00:14:01.831 --> 00:14:04.240
There was a certain set
of knowledge one

00:14:04.241 --> 00:14:07.210
required before one could
have their own website.

00:14:07.211 --> 00:14:09.290
This changed, however,
with the advent

00:14:09.291 --> 00:14:11.815
of Wix, Squarespace, WordPress.

00:14:11.816 --> 00:14:14.595
Without having
any knowledge of HTML,

00:14:14.596 --> 00:14:17.450
you could drag and drop
elements onto a canvas,

00:14:17.451 --> 00:14:20.670
and built out a website,
built out store.

00:14:20.671 --> 00:14:22.040
A common entrepreneur with

00:14:22.041 --> 00:14:24.180
no special computer
skills could get

00:14:24.181 --> 00:14:27.705
an online store up and
running in minutes,

00:14:27.706 --> 00:14:31.000
all because tools like Wix and

00:14:31.001 --> 00:14:34.715
Squarespace made creating
a website easy and fun.

00:14:34.716 --> 00:14:38.290
A website in today's day and
age isn't about a website,

00:14:38.291 --> 00:14:40.505
it's about having an identity.

00:14:40.506 --> 00:14:43.380
The onus is on
all the stalwarts of AI

00:14:43.381 --> 00:14:46.300
present here in this audience
to truly think,

00:14:46.301 --> 00:14:50.580
how can we highly functional
drag and drop tools with

00:14:50.581 --> 00:14:53.540
such easy user interface
that it could allow

00:14:53.541 --> 00:14:58.400
someone with zero coding skills
to deploy AI based apps?

00:14:58.560 --> 00:15:02.605
Sure, machine learning
and APT exist,

00:15:02.606 --> 00:15:06.235
but I challenge and
implore you to go further.

00:15:06.236 --> 00:15:09.800
I'm envisioning a platform
where a child could learn how

00:15:09.801 --> 00:15:10.910
to make an AI do

00:15:10.911 --> 00:15:13.855
an application even
before he writes code,

00:15:13.856 --> 00:15:19.010
simply by using drag and
drop tools on a canvas.

00:15:19.011 --> 00:15:20.130
What we are doing here is,

00:15:20.131 --> 00:15:24.105
taking the fear out of
AI, making it accessible.

00:15:24.106 --> 00:15:26.355
For proliferation to happen,

00:15:26.356 --> 00:15:30.145
any of the scary aspects of
AI need to be eliminated.

00:15:30.146 --> 00:15:32.660
We have to make AI a
natural part of our lives.

00:15:32.661 --> 00:15:34.740
We have to make it
fun and relatable.

00:15:34.741 --> 00:15:37.560
I'd like to propose
an extremely practical use case

00:15:37.561 --> 00:15:40.415
for AI that is sure to
hit every Indian heart.

