00:22:01.411 --> 00:22:04.710
I would like to propose
a two-way EMR system where

00:22:04.711 --> 00:22:06.380
the patient and doctor both have

00:22:06.381 --> 00:22:08.720
the ability to input data.

00:22:08.721 --> 00:22:10.930
Let's take a moment
to think majority

00:22:10.931 --> 00:22:12.880
of EMRs right now don't have

00:22:12.881 --> 00:22:15.490
the ability to have
a two-way conversation platform

00:22:15.491 --> 00:22:17.835
between the patient
and the doctor.

00:22:17.836 --> 00:22:22.265
Let's say you had a patient
come in for cancer treatment.

00:22:22.266 --> 00:22:24.035
As he starts his treatment,

00:22:24.036 --> 00:22:26.380
he's given a
standardized app that

00:22:26.381 --> 00:22:28.585
he downloads which
is tied up with

00:22:28.586 --> 00:22:30.090
his EMR number much like

00:22:30.091 --> 00:22:32.905
another number and he's
put on the cancer regimen.

00:22:32.906 --> 00:22:35.650
But as a part of
his healthcare treatment is also

00:22:35.651 --> 00:22:38.975
required to voluntarily
log his quality of sleep,

00:22:38.976 --> 00:22:41.500
his daily activities,
his daily diet.

00:22:41.501 --> 00:22:42.975
This one's for the data.

00:22:42.976 --> 00:22:46.165
Scientists in the room whose
wheels are already turning,

00:22:46.166 --> 00:22:49.540
now this data is being
collected through

00:22:49.541 --> 00:22:51.390
a mobile app on the phone and

00:22:51.391 --> 00:22:53.880
every time the patient goes
for his chemo treatment,

00:22:53.881 --> 00:22:55.710
the doctor is able
to generate analysis

00:22:55.711 --> 00:22:57.585
in real time to see what are

00:22:57.586 --> 00:23:00.235
the correlation between
lifestyle choices

00:23:00.236 --> 00:23:02.270
and prevalence of
certain types of cancer.

00:23:02.271 --> 00:23:04.460
This information is
currently not possible in

00:23:04.461 --> 00:23:07.570
real time as a two-way
EMR logging system,

00:23:07.571 --> 00:23:09.440
which allows the patient to log

00:23:09.441 --> 00:23:11.475
their lifestyles habits and give

00:23:11.476 --> 00:23:13.960
doctors real time access
into patients

00:23:13.961 --> 00:23:16.695
life is something that
hasn't been deployed.

00:23:16.696 --> 00:23:19.510
Doctors can see what is

00:23:19.511 --> 00:23:22.420
the correlation between diet
and certain types of cancer.

00:23:22.421 --> 00:23:24.020
Are certain types of cancers

00:23:24.021 --> 00:23:25.980
more prevalent in
certain zip codes?

00:23:25.981 --> 00:23:29.520
Are we seeing an increase
and outbreak of

00:23:29.521 --> 00:23:31.835
a certain subtype of
cancer coming from

00:23:31.836 --> 00:23:33.305
certain geographical region

00:23:33.306 --> 00:23:35.140
with certain lifestyle choices?

00:23:35.141 --> 00:23:37.195
I call this an Active EMR,

00:23:37.196 --> 00:23:38.855
where the patient actively

00:23:38.856 --> 00:23:40.965
takes part in logging
their daily habits,

00:23:40.966 --> 00:23:42.550
their calorie count,

00:23:42.551 --> 00:23:45.275
their activities of
the day, quality of sleep.

00:23:45.276 --> 00:23:48.320
Imagine the leap
healthcare can make when

00:23:48.321 --> 00:23:51.715
this data is cross-correlated
in real time.

00:23:51.716 --> 00:23:53.875
We're cutting through
all the red tape

00:23:53.876 --> 00:23:55.315
of gathering such data.

00:23:55.316 --> 00:23:57.335
You have an active
population of a billion

00:23:57.336 --> 00:24:00.440
plus participating in
a lifetime study that

00:24:00.441 --> 00:24:03.300
evolves and collects data that

00:24:03.301 --> 00:24:06.590
goes well beyond
just the confines of elaborate.

00:24:06.591 --> 00:24:08.955
Drones have become
a controversial topic.

